			<div class="content" id="post-content-4847004">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> I‘ll tell most of the story trough addenda.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
There is this organization who tries to recreate ancient creatures/gods trough genetic engineering.<br />
When the Foundation attacks one of its labs, they find it to be destroyed, with most of the information taken. Except for one creature. My SCP. The core idea is this:</p>
<ul>
<li>The SCP has traits of our ancestors (more hair etc).</li>
<li>The SCP can live for 25 years (the less years to live, the more heredity treats).</li>
<li>The SCP has the ability to psychologically affect other life forms. The affecting of other life forms seems to appear when the SCP is in a dangerous situation, and shows similarities to a defense mechanism. The SCP has faster reflexes then the average human, and appears to have a strong intuition for dangerous situations.</li>
<li>The SCP shows signs of affection towards a junior researcher</li>
</ul>
<p>Story:</p>
<p>The researchers didn't find something abnormal at first, so the security level was low. Then, an attempt to murder the SCP was made. It failed, but while in transport to a safer location, the SCP attacks its guards and walks away. Foundation personal see the SCP, but they aren't alarmed (see bullet-list point 3). The SCP walks into a lunch room filled with scientists, and murders senior researcher ???. After that, the involved Foundation personal are given a class E status, but are cleared for duty after intensive mental and psychical tests.</p>
<p>Wouldn't it be terrible, not knowing what‘s real and what’s fake? And when you’ve been fooled so many times that you thought you couldn't be fooled anymore, and then someone you started seeing as a friend betrays you? Well that’s what my SCP was thinking. The researcher it murdered was a spy for the organization, as is later discovered by the Foundation (she’s behind the murder attempt). My SCP recognized the voice, and thought that it was just another organization test. It leaves a note saying: ''I believed you'' (see bullet list point 4).</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<p>The idea is that there is an organization trying to recreate gods/mythological creatures from the past trough genetic engineering. Most of their attempts fail. They conduct, just like the Foundation, tests and contain the creatures.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The discovery of the SCP, the reveal of the spy and the SCP and the junior researcher their relationship.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br />
I want the story to focus on the emotional struggles of the SCP, and the organization.</p>

