<p>1) You need to seriously cut down the number of words; Elevator Pitch, Central Narrative, Hook, and Additional Notes need to be about 400 words. You can eliminate the additional notes: You don't need names and you may want to drop the idea for an organization (more on that below). That's your first 43 words.</p>
<p>2) You may want to look into the current GOI to find a group that works for you. The obvious suggestions are Herman Fuller's Circus of the Disquieting (using a program to create circus freaks), Prometheus Labs (one group could be interested in developing prehistoric individuals to test some theories), or even a Sarkic Cult. This will save you a lot of work and stress.</p>
<p>3) You need to define what the humanoid can do better. Telepathy and mental compulsion are different abilities; if it can read minds that works well with the story. A telepathic caveman is a great idea, by the way.</p>
<p>4) Other than that, it looks like you are looking more at a Tale than an actual article. If done as an article, including the information about the spy and its resolution needs to be included as a very clinical addendum, with just the facts. So keep that in mind if you end up writing this up.</p>
<p>5) Also, it's &quot;trait&quot;.</p>

